<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · river</p><h1 class="enc-title">Neva River</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Neva</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Neva is a short but powerful river of north-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a>, flowing about 74 kilometres from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lake-ladoga">Lake Ladoga</a> to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gulf-of-finland">Gulf of Finland</a>. It formed a key route between the Baltic and Novgorod and was long contested between Novgorod, later Russia, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweden">Sweden</a>; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexander-nevsky">Alexander Nevsky</a> won his name defeating the Swedes on it in 1240. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peter-the-great">Peter the Great</a> founded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saint-petersburg">Saint Petersburg</a> at its mouth in 1703.</p></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Prince Alexander Yaroslavich defeated a Swedish force on the <b>Neva</b> in 1240, earning the name Nevsky, and in 1242 defeated the Livonian branch of the Teutonic Order on the ice of Lake Peipus, the Battle on the Ice.</blockquote><a href="/empire/novgorod-republic">Novgorod Republic · Military</a></li><li><blockquote>Peter founded Saint Petersburg on the <b>Neva</b> in 1703, building a fleet and a new capital to which the court moved during the 1710s, and created a conscript army maintained by heavy taxation.</blockquote><a href="/empire/tsardom-of-russia">Tsardom of Russia · Decline &amp; Fall</a></li><li><blockquote>After that the grand princes fought chiefly as agents or rivals under Mongol overlordship, while Alexander Nevsky, before his accession, had defeated the Swedes on the <b>Neva</b> in 1240 and the Teutonic Knights on Lake Peipus in 1242.</blockquote><a href="/empire/vladimir-suzdal">Vladimir-Suzdal · Military</a></li><li><blockquote>After a cavalry charge failed on the icy cobbles, Nicholas at last had three guns fire grapeshot; rebels fleeing across the frozen <b>Neva</b> were shelled, and many sank as the ice broke.</blockquote><a href="/movement/decembrist-revolt">Decembrist revolt · Course of Events</a></li><li><blockquote>Sweden and the Novgorod Republic made peace at the fortress of Nöteborg, at the source of the <b>Neva</b>.</blockquote><a href="/today-in-history/august-12">12 August in history</a></li><li><blockquote>A Novgorodian army led by Alexander Nevsky, with Karelian allies, defeated a Swedish force that included Norwegian, Finnish and Tavastian troops on the <b>Neva River</b> near Ust-Izhora.</blockquote><a href="/today-in-history/july-15">15 July in history</a></li></ul></section>
